Vulkan constant buffers through dynamic uniform buffer descriptors. 0121's timers showed a constants descriptor set
allocated and written for nearly every draw (~5,000 a frame at the city spot, most of UpdateBindings' ~120-150 ns of
descriptor writes): any of the five constant buffers moving to a new upload offset needed a new set. The constants
set layout now uses VK_DESCRIPTOR_TYPE_UNIFORM_BUFFER_DYNAMIC with fixed ranges (the most each buffer holds), a set
only names the five upload buffers, and the offsets are passed when it is bound, so one set serves every draw whose
constants are in the same upload pages. The sets are kept per combination of buffers (few) in their own descriptor
pools until the upload pages are destroyed. VulkanUploadBufferPool takes a reserved tail that is never handed out,
so the fixed ranges stay within the page's buffer at any offset.

